# =============================================================================
#  CITATION.cff
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#  Citation File Format 1.2.0.
#  https://citation-file-format.github.io/
#
#  WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
#  Academic and policy work that uses this library needs to cite it, and the
#  people doing that work should not have to reconstruct a citation by hand
#  from a README. This file is machine-readable: GitHub renders a formatted
#  citation from it in the repository sidebar, Zenodo consumes it when minting
#  a DOI, and reference managers such as Zotero import it directly.
#
#  HOW TO VALIDATE IT
#      pip install cffconvert
#      cffconvert --validate
#      cffconvert -f bibtex
#      cffconvert -f apalike
#
#  MAINTENANCE RULE
#  The `version` and `date-released` keys below must match the current release.
#  The release workflow checks this and refuses to publish if they have drifted
#  from pyproject.toml.
#
#  SPDX-License-Identifier: EUPL-1.2
# =============================================================================

cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this library in a publication, a curriculum or a policy document,
  please cite it as below.

title: >-
  biotechnology: a machine-readable, dual-register taxonomy of the
  colour-coded branches of biotechnology

abstract: >-
  Biotechnology is conventionally divided into ten colour-coded branches: red
  for medicine, green for agriculture, white for industry, blue for marine,
  yellow for food, grey for environment, brown for arid lands, gold for
  bioinformatics, dark for biosecurity and purple for law and ethics. That
  scheme is taught widely and used in policy documents, but has never existed
  as structured, queryable, citable data. This library provides it: ten
  branches and eighty-five subtypes, each described twice, once in a technical
  register for specialists and once in plain language for the parliamentary
  committees, procurement officers, journalists and students who make or shape
  decisions about the field. Each record additionally carries measurable
  metrics with units and evidence grades, links to computable formula modules,
  a dated history including its failures, its governance position in controlled
  vocabularies, applicable regulations and standards, and typed
  cross-references to the rest of the taxonomy. The package has no runtime
  dependencies, is fully typed, and validates every cross-reference on every
  commit.

type: software

authors:
  - given-names: Gustav Olaf Yunus
    family-names: Laitinen-Fredriksson Lundstrom-Imanov
    email: yunus.imanov@metropolia.fi
    affiliation: >-
      School of Information and Communication Technology, Metropolia
      University of Applied Sciences, Karaportti 2, 02610 Espoo, Finland
    country: FI

repository-code: https://github.com/olaflaitinen/biotechnology
url: https://github.com/olaflaitinen/biotechnology
repository-artifact: https://pypi.org/project/biotechnology/

version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-09-02

license: EUPL-1.2
license-url: https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/eupl/eupl-text-eupl-12

keywords:
