# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#  Works that shaped the design of this library. These are not the scientific
#  references for its content, which live in BIBLIOGRAPHY.md and in
#  src/biotechnology/refs/, but the methodological sources for how research
#  software and research data ought to be built and described.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
references:
  - type: article
    title: >-
      The FAIR Guiding Principles for scientific data management and
      stewardship
    authors:
      - family-names: Wilkinson
        given-names: Mark D.
    year: 2016
    journal: Scientific Data
    volume: 3
    doi: 10.1038/sdata.2016.18
    notes: >-
      The findable, accessible, interoperable and reusable principles that the
      export formats, stable identifiers and cross-reference validation in
      this library are designed to satisfy.

  - type: report
    title: Transforming our world, the 2030 Agenda for Sustainable Development
    authors:
      - name: United Nations General Assembly
    year: 2015
    notes: >-
      Source of the seventeen Sustainable Development Goals referenced by the
      sdgs field of every subtype record.

  - type: generic
    title: Citation File Format
    authors:
      - family-names: Druskat
        given-names: Stephan
    year: 2021
    doi: 10.5281/zenodo.1003149
    notes: The specification this file conforms to.

